config MTK_VCU
	bool "MediaTek VCU bridge for the vendor video daemon"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on MTK_CMDQ=y
	select VIDEOBUF2_CORE
	help
	  Provides /dev/vcu, the kernel side of the MediaTek vendor video
	  stack (vpud). It relays IPI messages between video codec drivers
	  and vpud, allocates DMA working buffers for the daemon, maps the
	  codec register windows described by the "mediatek-vcu" DT node
	  and executes the daemon's GCE command lists through the mtk-cmdq
	  mailbox.

	  The driver stays inert unless the kernel is booted with
	  mtk_vcu.enable=1.

	  If unsure, say N.
